2dcf48646d483361cd0c2d970fdafedb8bb4abbb.text:
{
  "title": "Perceived Utility in RAG Outputs",
  "summary": "Liu et al. (2023a) introduce 'perceived utility value' as a metric independent of retrieved passages, defining 'Useful' (ISUSE) as perceived utility. This concept is equivalent to 'plausibility' as defined by Menick et al. (2022). Supported output (ISSUP) is cited by both Menick et al. (2022) and Bohnet et al. (2022). Liu et al. find that longer, more fluent generation leads to more unsupported claims, linking fluency with reduced factual support. Together, these entities establish a framework where perceived utility drives response helpfulness, even when unsupported."
}

